A||N||6||AusFiero||How's this for an engine swap||||6||
Z||000000||AusFiero||09-25-2001||06:41 AM||||Well today after someone suggested on the forum that maybe I should use one of the cool exotic engines available here in Aus instead of turboing the 2.8 I came across a feasible swap. Well seems feasible by measurements so far and I will talk to my mechanic. <P>How does a turbocharged, quad cammed 3.0 ltr V6 pushing out 285 HP and 278 ft/pd torque @ 6500 RPM sound. It is a Nissan engine from a Nissan Leopard and looks like it will fit no worries. Time for more measuring. Plus the price is outstanding. $1695 ($US850) for a complete front cut of the car it is in which will give me the wiring harness, ECM, radiator and many other bits needed. This engine can be easily pushed to 400 HP cheaply the importer tells me. Is kinda cheaper than turboing the 2.8 even with mods needed to fit it. <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||6
